# Testing Standards

## Test Hierarchy

```
Unit Tests (*Test.java)      → Fast, no I/O, mock dependencies
Integration Tests (*IT.java) → Real dependencies via Testcontainers
```

## Unit Test Pattern

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class PipelineServiceTest {
    @Mock PipelineRepository repository;
    @Mock EventPublisher publisher;
    @InjectMocks PipelineService service;
    
    @Test
    void createPipeline_validInput_returnsPipeline() {
        // Given
        var command = new CreatePipelineCommand("ETL Job", definition);
        when(repository.save(any())).thenAnswer(inv -> inv.getArgument(0));
        
        // When
        var result = service.createPipeline(command);
        
        // Then
        assertThat(result.getName()).isEqualTo("ETL Job");
        verify(publisher).publish(any(PipelineCreatedEvent.class));
    }
    
    @Test
    void createPipeline_invalidDefinition_throwsValidationException() {
        // Given
        var command = new CreatePipelineCommand("", null);
        
        // When/Then
        assertThatThrownBy(() -> service.createPipeline(command))
            .isInstanceOf(ValidationException.class)
            .hasMessageContaining("definition");
    }
}
```

## Integration Test Pattern

```java
@SpringBootTest
@Testcontainers
@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = Replace.NONE)
class PipelineServiceIT {
    
    @Container
    static PostgreSQLContainer<?> postgres = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:16-alpine");
    
    @DynamicPropertySource
    static void configureProperties(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
        registry.add("spring.datasource.url", postgres::getJdbcUrl);
        registry.add("spring.datasource.username", postgres::getUsername);
        registry.add("spring.datasource.password", postgres::getPassword);
    }
    
    @Autowired PipelineService service;
    @Autowired PipelineRepository repository;
    
    @BeforeEach
    void setUp() {
        repository.deleteAll();
    }
    
    @Test
    void createAndRetrievePipeline() {
        // Given
        var command = new CreatePipelineCommand("ETL Job", validDefinition());
        
        // When
        var created = service.createPipeline(command);
        var retrieved = service.getPipeline(created.getId());
        
        // Then
        assertThat(retrieved).isPresent();
        assertThat(retrieved.get().getName()).isEqualTo("ETL Job");
    }
}
```

## Test Naming Convention

```java
// Pattern: methodName_condition_expectedResult
void createPipeline_validInput_returnsPipeline()
void createPipeline_nullName_throwsValidationException()
void triggerExecution_pipelineNotFound_throws404()
```

## What to Test

| Layer | What to Test | How |
|-------|--------------|-----|
| Domain | Business logic, state transitions | Unit tests |
| Service | Orchestration, transactions | Unit + Integration |
| Repository | Queries, RLS enforcement | Integration with Testcontainers |
| Controller | Request/response mapping, validation | @WebMvcTest |
| Kafka | Message serialization, consumer logic | @EmbeddedKafka |

## Test Coverage Rules

- New code: minimum 80% line coverage
- State machines: 100% transition coverage
- Happy path + all error paths must be tested
- Never skip tests with @Disabled without an issue link
